{"name":"Limonite Brown","hex":"#4b4433","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limonite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several natural hydrous iron oxides; often a mixture of goethite and hematite with clays and manganese oxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limonite"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limonite","blocks":[{"text":"Limonite is an iron ore consisting of a mixture of hydrated iron(III) oxide-hydroxides in varying composition. The generic formula is frequently written as FeO(OH)·nH2O, although this is not entirely accurate as the ratio of oxide to hydroxide can vary quite widely. Limonite is one of the three principal iron ores, the others being hematite and magnetite, and has been mined for the production of iron since at least 400 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/LimoniteUSGOV.jpg/330px-LimoniteUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limonite","wikidata":"Q193565"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg/500px-Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg?ut